WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.608
Everything that changes on the XRP Ledger happens through a transaction: a signed instruction from an account.

2
00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:10.748
This video shows how to read what happened to one.

3
00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:14.743
A Payment sends XRP or a token.

4
00:00:14.743 --> 00:00:18.592
OfferCreate places a trade on the built-in exchange.

5
00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:25.570
TrustSet opens a trust line so an account can hold a token, and AccountSet changes an account's settings.

6
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.950
Every transaction pays a tiny fee in XRP.

7
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:34.596
The fee is destroyed, not paid to anyone, which protects the network from spam.

8
00:00:36.296 --> 00:00:40.962
When a transaction is first submitted, the server gives a tentative result.

9
00:00:40.962 --> 00:00:48.179
It becomes final only when the transaction is in a validated ledger, and the final result is stored in its metadata.

10
00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:51.399
So never treat the first answer as the last.

11
00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:53.791
NOSHASHI reads validated ledgers only.

12
00:00:55.491 --> 00:01:00.163
A result starting with t e s means success: the transaction did what it said.

13
00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:07.316
A result starting with t e c means it failed but was still recorded in the ledger, and the fee was charged.

14
00:01:07.316 --> 00:01:08.507
Nothing else moved.

15
00:01:08.957 --> 00:01:17.661
Results starting with t e f, t e l, t e m or t e r mean the transaction was not applied at all, and no fee was charged.

16
00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:20.126
One warning.

17
00:01:20.126 --> 00:01:25.547
A payment can say success and still deliver only a tiny part of the amount it states.

18
00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:27.684
That is a partial payment.

19
00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:31.381
The figure to trust is delivered amount, in the metadata.

20
00:01:31.381 --> 00:01:33.976
Video five shows a real case on mainnet.
